%9Setting:%9

    term_notify (choice: off, auto, osc9, osc777; default: off)
    term_notify_text (boolean; default: ON)

%9Description:%9

    Shows a desktop notification through the terminal for every mention
    (see /HELP MENTIONS: a private message or action, a NOTICE to you, a
    DCC CHAT message or a channel hilight), but only while the terminal
    reports it is not focused. At most one notification is sent in three
    seconds.

    OFF sends nothing. AUTO sends notifications when the terminal is known
    to show them:

        - iTerm2 and kitty get OSC 9,
        - WezTerm, Ghostty and foot get OSC 777.

    For any other terminal AUTO sends nothing. OSC9 and OSC777 send that
    sequence whatever the terminal is.

    Whether the terminal is focused is learnt from the focus reports
    (ESC [ I and ESC [ O) that erssi asks the terminal for while
    notifications are on; until the first report the terminal counts as
    focused. When term_notify sends nothing, focus reports are not asked
    for at all.

    Inside tmux the sequence is passed through to the outer terminal. tmux
    needs "set -g focus-events on" (for the focus reports) and
    "set -g allow-passthrough on" (for the notification) in tmux.conf. The
    outer terminal is recognised from LC_TERMINAL, KITTY_WINDOW_ID,
    GHOSTTY_RESOURCES_DIR or WEZTERM_PANE.

    Inside GNU Screen (STY is set) AUTO never sends notifications; OSC9
    and OSC777 send the sequence as it is.

    The notification shows where the entry came from and the nick, and
    with term_notify_text ON also the text. The notification may be shown
    on the lock screen or stored by the desktop: set term_notify_text OFF
    to leave the text out. Control characters are removed from everything
    that is sent, and long texts are cut.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET term_notify auto
    /SET term_notify osc9
    /SET term_notify_text off

%9See also:%9

    SET, MENTIONS
